<item>
            <title>[IGNITE-4592] .NET: Binary enums are handled incorrectly</title>
                <link>https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/IGNITE-4592</link>
                <project id="12315922" key="IGNITE">Ignite</project>
                    <description>&lt;ul&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;BinaryEnum is represented as &lt;tt&gt;int typeId&lt;/tt&gt; + &lt;tt&gt;int value&lt;/tt&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;BinaryEnumArray is represented as &lt;tt&gt;int typeId&lt;/tt&gt; + &lt;tt&gt;int[] value&lt;/tt&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;


&lt;p&gt;In most cases we handle this incorrectly, using only &lt;tt&gt;int value&lt;/tt&gt;:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;&lt;tt&gt;BinaryObjectBuilder.WriteAsPredefined&lt;/tt&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;&lt;tt&gt;BinarySystemHandlers.*EnumArray&lt;/tt&gt;&lt;br/&gt;
etc&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;


&lt;p&gt;Add tests thich verify that .NET binary enum handling is consistent with Java.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
                <environment></environment>
        <key id="13037073">IGNITE-4592</key>
